<section id="home" class="section active"><div class="bigquestion"><div class="ey">HOW TO USE THIS DASHBOARD</div><h2>Follow the story in order.</h2><p class="muted">You do not need to understand medical jargon first. The dashboard starts with what happened, then shows what each report means, what each medicine changes inside your body, what ILMB is trying to change in parallel, and which measurements tell us whether the plan is working.</p></div><div class="stepper" style="margin-top:14px">
<div class="step" data-go="reports"><b>01</b><strong>Read my reports</strong><span>What did the MRI, MRA, CT and blood tests actually show?</span></div><div class="step" data-go="event"><b>02</b><strong>Understand what happened</strong><span>Which artery, which brain area and which functions were affected?</span></div><div class="step" data-go="meds"><b>03</b><strong>Understand my medicines</strong><span>Target → body pathway → benefit → collateral burden.</span></div><div class="step" data-go="paths"><b>04</b><strong>Compare the two paths</strong><span>What does Pharma control directly and what can ILMB change by another route?</span></div><div class="step" data-go="ilmb"><b>05</b><strong>Follow my ILMB plan</strong><span>What do I do now, what is still missing and what comes next?</span></div><div class="step" data-go="labs"><b>06</b><strong>Measure the outputs</strong><span>LOINC keeps every lab identity exact in the background.</span></div><div class="step" data-go="daily"><b>07</b><strong>Add my own inputs</strong><span>BP, HR, food, symptoms, movement and observations.</span></div><div class="step" data-go="review"><b>08</b><strong>Decide from my response</strong><span>KEEP · MODIFY · INVESTIGATE · ESCALATE.</span></div></div>
<div class="grid g4" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="card kpi"><div class="muted small">Triglycerides</div><div><span class="v">301</span> mg/dL</div><span class="badge bad">high</span></div><div class="card kpi"><div class="muted small">25-OH Vitamin D</div><div><span class="v">13.9</span> ng/mL</div><span class="badge bad">low</span></div><div class="card kpi"><div class="muted small">Platelets</div><div><span class="v">133</span> ×10³/µL</div><span class="badge watch">context</span></div><div class="card kpi"><div class="muted small">HbA1c</div><div><span class="v">5.8</span>%</div><span class="badge watch">watch</span></div></div>
<div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY CORE GOALS</div><h2>What are we protecting?</h2><div class="call"><b>1.</b> Prevent another vascular event.<br><b>2.</b> Preserve and improve brain and motor function.<br><b>3.</b> Reduce avoidable treatment burden while preserving established benefit.<br><b>4.</b> Learn my own response instead of assuming I behave like an average patient.</div></div><div class="card"><div class="ey">CONTROL ROOM</div><h2>Known vs missing</h2><p><span class="badge ok">KNOWN</span> stroke location, historical weakness, medicine list, major labs.</p><p><span class="badge watch">MISSING</span> current right-MCA lumen/flow/collaterals/perfusion, quantitative motor baseline, current repeat labs, exact cod-liver-oil composition.</p><p><span class="badge unknown">BLOCKED CLAIM</span> direct non-drug P2Y12 or COX-1/TXA₂ equivalence.</p></div></div></section>

<section id="reports" class="section"><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY SOURCE REPORTS</div><h2>What each report told us</h2><div class="report"><div class="date">23 Aug 2024</div><div><b>MRI Brain</b><br><span class="muted">Multiple fresh non-haemorrhagic infarcts in the right fronto-parieto-temporal region.</span><p class="small">Meaning: several areas supplied by the right cerebral circulation were injured by loss of blood supply.</p></div><span class="badge bad tag">ACUTE EVENT</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">23 Aug 2024</div><div><b>MRA Brain</b><br><span class="muted">High-grade right middle cerebral artery occlusion from origin with severe paucity of distal branches.</span><p class="small">Meaning: the main blood-supply route to a large right-brain territory was severely compromised.</p></div><span class="badge bad tag">VESSEL</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">23 Aug 2024</div><div><b>Cardiology / echo</b><br><span class="muted">LVEF approximately 60%; no readable major chamber clot or major structural abnormality recorded.</span><p class="small">Meaning: the available report did not identify an obvious major cardiac source in that study.</p></div><span class="badge ok tag">CONTEXT</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">21 Jul 2025</div><div><b>MRI / MRA follow-up</b><br><span class="muted">Chronic right lacunar infarcts and old internal-capsule sequela; right MCA M1 still showed no flow; faint M2 enhancement questioned as collateral.</span><p class="small">Meaning: the artery still looked severely abnormal, while some alternative collateral supply may have been present but was not quantified.</p></div><span class="badge watch tag">PERSISTENT</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">26 Jul 2025</div><div><b>Clinical follow-up</b><br><span class="muted">Conscious, oriented, normal speech, no recorded deficit.</span><p class="small">Meaning: function had recovered much more than the vessel image alone would suggest. This makes compensation/collateral flow/neuroplasticity important questions.</p></div><span class="badge ok tag">FUNCTION</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">05 May 2026</div><div><b>Laboratory panel</b><br><span class="muted">TG 301, ALT 81, creatinine 1.27, eGFR 72, potassium 5.3, platelets 133k, 25-OH-D 13.9, TSH 5.386, HbA1c 5.8.</span><p class="small">Meaning: recurrence risk, treatment safety, liver/kidney/electrolyte context and nutrient state all need to be tracked together.</p></div><span class="badge watch tag">BODY STATE</span></div><div class="report"><div class="date">31 Jul 2026</div><div><b>Plain CT Brain</b><br><span class="muted">Old right-sided infarcts/internal-capsule sequela; no acute infarct, haemorrhage or mass.</span><p class="small">Meaning: no new acute lesion was seen, but plain CT cannot tell us current MCA lumen, collateral reserve or regional perfusion.</p></div><span class="badge ok tag">NO ACUTE LESION</span></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h3>My own report notes</h3><textarea id="reportNotes" class="notearea" placeholder="Add what another report or doctor told you, with date if possible."></textarea></div></section>

<section id="event" class="section"><div class="grid g2"><div class="card"><div class="ey">WHAT HAPPENED</div><h2>The stroke chain</h2><div class="flow"><span class="node">Right MCA flow ↓</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">O₂ / glucose delivery ↓</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">ATP failure</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">brain tissue injury</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">left weakness / numbness</span></div><p class="muted small">The right brain controls much of the left side of the body. The initial recorded power was 3/5.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="ey">WHY RECOVERY MATTERS</div><h2>Structure and function diverged</h2><p>The artery remained severely abnormal on later MRA, yet later clinical notes recorded normal speech and no deficit.</p><div class="call">That means the next question is not only “is the artery open?” but also “how is the brain being supplied and how has the network adapted?”</div><div class="pillrow" style="margin-top:10px"><span class="pill">collateral circulation</span><span class="pill">regional perfusion</span><span class="pill">neuroplasticity</span><span class="pill">motor network compensation</span></div></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="ey">MISSING MEASUREMENT</div><h2>What still needs to be established</h2><p><b>Current right-MCA lumen / flow / collaterals / tissue perfusion.</b> This is not answered by the 2026 plain CT. A focused stroke/vascular review should explicitly answer these questions and also confirm why dual antiplatelet therapy remains indicated and for how long.</p></div></section>

<section id="body" class="section"><div class="card"><div class="ey">EXPLORE MY BODY</div><h2>Tap a system to see why it matters for me</h2><div class="systems"><div class="system" onclick="openSys('brain')"><b>Brain / right MCA</b><div class="muted small">Perfusion · collaterals · plasticity · recovery</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('blood')"><b>Platelets / thrombosis</b><div class="muted small">P2Y12 · COX-1/TXA₂ · fibrinolysis</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('heart')"><b>Heart / vessels</b><div class="muted small">BP · HR · vascular resistance · endothelium</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('liver')"><b>Liver / lipids</b><div class="muted small">TG · LDL · VLDL · ALT</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('gut')"><b>Gut / food chemistry</b><div class="muted small">substrates · SCFA · metabolic / immune signals</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('kidney')"><b>Kidney / electrolytes</b><div class="muted small">creatinine · eGFR · potassium · safety</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('motor')"><b>Muscle / movement</b><div class="muted small">force · gait · dexterity · motor learning</div></div><div class="system" onclick="openSys('thyroid')"><b>Thyroid / metabolic context</b><div class="muted small">TSH · free T4 · energy / metabolism</div></div></div><label>My body notes</label><textarea id="bodyNotes"></textarea></div></section>

<section id="meds" class="section"><div class="call"><b>Read each medicine in five parts:</b> what it targets → what changes inside the body → how that treats the problem → what collateral burden can occur → what ILMB can or cannot change by another route.</div><div id="medList" class="grid g2" style="margin-top:14px"></div></section>

<section id="paths" class="section"><div class="card"><div class="ey">TWO PATHS · ONE REQUIRED BODY OUTPUT</div><h2>We compare benefit and burden separately</h2><div class="two"><div class="card"><div class="ey">PHARMA</div><div class="formula">P = Bₚ − Hₚ</div><p class="small muted">Benefit from the medicine minus collateral treatment burden.</p></div><div class="arrow">⇄</div><div class="card"><div class="ey">ILMB</div><div class="formula">I = Bᵢ − Hᵢ</div><p class="small muted">Benefit from food/movement/rehab/sleep/gut/environmental routes minus their own burden.</p></div></div><div class="call warn" style="margin-top:12px"><b>Goal:</b> where demonstrable, achieve the same required physiological output with lower avoidable burden. This does <b>not</b> mean pretending a food or exercise intervention blocks the same receptor as a drug.</div></div><div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="card"><h3>Prevent platelet-rich arterial thrombosis</h3><p><b>Pharma:</b> clopidogrel directly inhibits P2Y12; aspirin directly inhibits COX-1/TXA₂.</p><p><b>ILMB:</b> can work on endothelial function, BP, metabolic load, fibrinolytic background and other upstream/downstream states.</p><span class="badge bad">DIRECT RECEPTOR EQUIVALENCE NOT ESTABLISHED</span></div><div class="card"><h3>Control BP / cardiac demand</h3><p><b>Pharma:</b> amlodipine lowers vascular resistance; atenolol lowers β1-driven HR/contractility.</p><p><b>ILMB:</b> conditioning, autonomic state, sleep, fluid/sodium context and endothelial function can move the same measured outputs.</p><span class="badge watch">PARTIAL FUNCTIONAL EQUIVALENCE</span></div><div class="card"><h3>Reduce triglyceride / lipid burden</h3><p><b>Pharma:</b> atorvastatin changes HMGCR/LDL clearance; fenofibrate activates PPARα and TG clearance.</p><p><b>ILMB:</b> reduce hepatic substrate load, change food chemistry/gut absorption and increase muscle utilisation.</p><span class="badge watch">PARTIAL</span></div><div class="card"><h3>Restore motor function</h3><p><b>Pharma:</b> current medicines do not directly retrain the motor network.</p><p><b>ILMB:</b> task practice, strength, gait, dexterity and deficit-specific rehabilitation can directly target function.</p><span class="badge ok">MEASURE FUNCTION DIRECTLY</span></div></div></section>

<section id="ilmb" class="section"><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY ILMB TREATMENT METHOD</div><h2>Step by step — what happens now</h2><div class="phase"><b>STEP 1</b><div><strong>Protect what is already working.</strong><p class="small muted">Continue current prescribed medicines. The dashboard does not instruct withdrawal. Record actual symptoms or side effects rather than assuming them.</p></div><span class="badge ok">NOW</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 2</b><div><strong>Define the current vascular state.</strong><p class="small muted">Establish current right-MCA lumen/flow, collateral circulation and regional perfusion, and document the present indication/duration for aspirin + clopidogrel.</p></div><span class="badge bad">MISSING</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 3</b><div><strong>Repeat the unresolved body-state measurements.</strong><p class="small muted">Fasting lipids, fasting glucose, CBC/platelets, ALT/AST/GGT, creatinine/eGFR, potassium, TSH + free T4, 25-OH-D, urinalysis + urine ACR.</p></div><span class="badge watch">72 HOURS</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 4</b><div><strong>Quantify function instead of saying “recovered”.</strong><p class="small muted">Bilateral grip, arm/leg strength, 10-m walk, sit-to-stand, dexterity, balance, ROM and tone.</p></div><span class="badge watch">7 DAYS</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 5</b><div><strong>Capture actual input chemistry.</strong><p class="small muted">Three normal weighed days of food/drink/supplements. ILMB converts grams → food composition → chemical input → pathway relevance. No generic “healthy diet” assumption.</p></div><span class="badge watch">3 DAYS</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 6</b><div><strong>Build the personalised intervention.</strong><p class="small muted">Food chemistry, movement dose, sleep/autonomic work, rehabilitation and other modalities are switched on only for the body nodes that are actually abnormal.</p></div><span class="badge unknown">AFTER BASELINE</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 7</b><div><strong>Hold the input steady long enough to measure response.</strong><p class="small muted">Do not change five things every day. Record delivered dose/exposure so the body response can be attributed.</p></div><span class="badge unknown">CONTROLLED PERIOD</span></div><div class="phase"><b>STEP 8</b><div><strong>Re-measure and calculate Nilesh’s own response.</strong><p class="small muted">Example: ΔTG after a documented food/activity input, or ΔBP after a defined intervention.</p><div class="formula">k = Δ measured output ÷ delivered input</div></div><span class="badge ok">PERSONAL MATH</span></div></div><div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="card"><h3>What ILMB is actively targeting now</h3><div class="pillrow"><span class="pill">vascular/endothelial state</span><span class="pill">BP / HR</span><span class="pill">TG / lipid metabolism</span><span class="pill">liver safety context</span><span class="pill">vitamin D / nutrient gaps</span><span class="pill">motor function</span><span class="pill">sleep/autonomic state</span><span class="pill">gut-metabolic inputs</span></div></div><div class="card"><h3>What ILMB is not claiming</h3><p class="small">No direct natural P2Y12 replacement. No direct natural COX-1/TXA₂ replacement. No invented microbiome coefficients. No automatic food/supplement dose from one lab value. No “stop medicine because numbers improved” rule.</p></div></div></section>

<section id="labs" class="section"><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY NUMBERS · LOINC IN THE BACKGROUND</div><h2>Every measurement has one exact identity</h2><p class="muted small">You see plain English. ILMB stores the laboratory identity using LOINC so “triglycerides”, for example, cannot silently become a different test or specimen.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Measurement</th><th>Known value</th><th>LOINC</th><th>Why it matters for me</th><th>New value</th><th>Date</th><th>My note</th></tr></thead><tbody id="labRows"></tbody></table></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><details><summary>Show me what LOINC is doing behind the scenes</summary><p class="small muted">LOINC is not a treatment. It is an identity system for measurements. ILMB uses it to connect a patient result to the correct formula, pathway and repeat measurement without relying on fuzzy text matching. The governed crosswalk only computes when the endpoint identity is approved.</p></details></div></section>

<section id="daily" class="section"><div class="grid g2"><div class="card"><h2>BP / HR</h2><p class="muted small">Same conditions morning and evening for 7 days. Atenolol can blunt heart-rate response, so generic target-HR formulas are not used for exercise dosing.</p><div id="bpLog"></div><button class="btn" onclick="addBP()">+ Add BP / HR</button></div><div class="card"><h2>Actual symptoms / side effects</h2><label>Bleeding or bruising</label><select id="bleeding"><option>No</option><option>Mild</option><option>Moderate</option><option>Severe / urgent</option></select><label>Dizziness</label><select id="dizziness"><option>No</option><option>Mild</option><option>Moderate</option><option>Severe</option></select><label>Fatigue</label><select id="fatigue"><option>No</option><option>Mild</option><option>Moderate</option><option>Severe</option></select><label>Muscle pain / weakness</label><select id="muscle"><option>No</option><option>Mild</option><option>Moderate</option><option>Severe</option></select><label>Anything else</label><textarea id="symptomNotes"></textarea></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>3-day weighed food / drink record</h2><div class="call">Enter normal intake. ILMB needs the real input, not an artificially “perfect” day.</div><div id="foodLog" style="margin-top:10px"></div><button class="btn" onclick="addFood()">+ Add food / drink</button><details class="behind"><summary>What happens to this food data?</summary><p class="small muted">grams / mL → IFCT/USDA food composition → nutrient/chemical identity → ChEBI where mapped → Reactome/pathway relevance → patient-specific required output. If a coefficient is unknown, ILMB keeps the gap open instead of inventing a number.</p></details></div></section>

<section id="motor" class="section"><div class="grid g2"><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY FUNCTION VECTOR</div><h2>Measure recovery, do not assume it</h2><label>Left grip (kg)</label><input id="leftGrip" type="number" step="0.1"><label>Right grip (kg)</label><input id="rightGrip" type="number" step="0.1"><label>10-m walk (seconds)</label><input id="walk10" type="number" step="0.1"><label>5× sit-to-stand (seconds)</label><input id="sitstand" type="number" step="0.1"><label>Left arm strength / note</label><input id="leftArm"><label>Right arm strength / note</label><input id="rightArm"><label>Left leg strength / note</label><input id="leftLeg"><label>Right leg strength / note</label><input id="rightLeg"></div><div class="card"><h2>What turns rehab modules on?</h2><p class="small muted">If a deficit is zero, that modality stays off. If a specific problem is present, ILMB selects from task practice, strength, gait training, dexterity work, mirror therapy, FES/NMES, CIMT, AFO/assistive devices or other relevant modalities based on the measured deficit.</p><label>What I want to improve</label><textarea id="motorGoals" class="notearea"></textarea></div></div></section>

<section id="review" class="section"><div class="grid g2"><div class="card"><div class="ey">REVIEW</div><h2>Every intervention gets a decision</h2><div id="decisionRows"></div></div><div class="card"><div class="ey">MY RESPONSE</div><h2>What changed?</h2><div class="formula">k = Δ output ÷ delivered input</div><p class="small muted">This is the core idea: the dashboard should learn Nilesh’s own response rather than assume a population-average coefficient.</p><label>Response notes</label><textarea id="responseNotes" class="notearea"></textarea></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Completion checklist</h2><div class="checklist" id="checklist"></div></div></section>

<section id="evidence" class="section"><div class="grid g2"><div class="card"><div class="ey">IDENTITY LAYER</div><h2>What LOINC and ChEBI are doing</h2><p><b>LOINC</b> identifies the exact measurement: triglycerides, ALT, potassium, platelets, vitamin D, etc.</p><p><b>ChEBI</b> identifies chemicals and biochemical entities: butyrate, tryptophan, nitric oxide, arachidonic acid, cholesterol, glucose and many others.</p><p><b>Reactome</b> links those entities into biological reactions and pathways.</p><div class="flow"><span class="node">Patient result</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">LOINC identity</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">body state</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">ChEBI chemical</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">Reactome pathway</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">intervention</span><span class="sep">→</span><span class="node">remeasure</span></div></div><div class="card"><div class="ey">EXAMPLES</div><h2>Patient view vs database view</h2><div class="metric"><span>Triglycerides</span><span class="badge">LOINC 2571-8</span></div><div class="metric"><span>HbA1c</span><span class="badge">LOINC 4548-4</span></div><div class="metric"><span>ALT</span><span class="badge">LOINC 1742-6</span></div><div class="metric"><span>Platelets</span><span class="badge">LOINC 777-3</span></div><div class="metric"><span>25-OH Vitamin D</span><span class="badge">LOINC 62292-8</span></div><div class="metric"><span>Butyrate</span><span class="badge">ChEBI 17968</span></div><div class="metric"><span>L-tryptophan</span><span class="badge">ChEBI 16828</span></div><div class="metric"><span>Nitric oxide</span><span class="badge">ChEBI 16480</span></div><div class="metric"><span>Arachidonic acid</span><span class="badge">ChEBI 15843</span></div></div></div><div class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="ey">UNKNOWN ≠ ZERO</div><h2>Open gaps that must remain visible</h2><div class="pillrow"><span class="pill">current MCA perfusion</span><span class="pill">direct non-drug P2Y12 equivalence</span><span class="pill">direct non-drug COX-1/TXA₂ equivalence</span><span class="pill">current 3-day food chemistry</span><span class="pill">current motor vector</span><span class="pill">exact cod-liver-oil composition</span><span class="pill">patient-specific response coefficients</span></div></div></section>

</main></div><div id="drawer" class="drawer"><button class="close" onclick="closeDrawer()">×</button><div id="drawerContent"></div></div><script>
const labs=[['tg','Triglycerides',301,'mg/dL','2571-8','Metabolic / vascular thrombogenic load'],['hba1c','HbA1c',5.8,'%','4548-4','Long-term glycemic state'],['alt','ALT',81,'U/L','1742-6','Liver safety / metabolic context'],['creatinine','Creatinine',1.27,'mg/dL','2160-0','Kidney safety'],['egfr','eGFR',72,'mL/min/1.73m²','—','Kidney function'],['potassium','Potassium',5.3,'mmol/L','2823-3','Electrolyte safety'],['platelets','Platelets',133,'×10³/µL','777-3','Antiplatelet safety context'],['vitd','25-OH Vitamin D',13.9,'ng/mL','62292-8','Nutrient state'],['tsh','TSH',5.386,'µIU/mL','3016-3','Thyroid state'],['ldl','LDL-C',76.08,'mg/dL','13457-7','Atherogenic lipid state'],['hdl','HDL-C',40,'mg/dL','2085-9','Lipid state'],['glucose','Random glucose',92,'mg/dL','2345-7','Glucose state']];
const meds=[
{time:'Morning',name:'Amlodac AT',dose:'Amlodipine 5 mg + Atenolol 50 mg',target:'L-type calcium channel + β1 receptor',path:'Amlodipine: vascular smooth-muscle Ca²⁺ entry ↓ → arterial resistance ↓. Atenolol: β1 signaling ↓ → HR / contractility / renin-related drive ↓.',treat:'Lowers blood pressure and cardiac workload.',harm:'Possible edema, dizziness, hypotension, bradycardia and fatigue. Atenolol can blunt exercise heart-rate response.',ilmb:'Endothelial / vascular conditioning, autonomic state, sleep, fluid-sodium context and fitness can move BP/HR by different routes.',output:'SBP / DBP / resting HR',status:'PARTIAL FUNCTIONAL EQUIVALENCE'},
{time:'Afternoon',name:'Clopilet',dose:'Clopidogrel 75 mg',target:'P2Y12 platelet receptor',path:'Prodrug activation → irreversible P2Y12 blockade → ADP amplification ↓ → αIIbβ3 activation ↓ → fibrinogen bridging ↓ → platelet aggregation ↓.',treat:'Reduces propagation of platelet-rich arterial thrombus.',harm:'Normal hemostasis is also reduced, so bleeding / bruising burden can rise.',ilmb:'Improve endothelial function, metabolic load and fibrinolytic background. No direct non-drug P2Y12 equivalent is established.',output:'P2Y12/PRU or ADP aggregation if clinically ordered',status:'DIRECT GAP REMAINS'},
{time:'Afternoon',name:'Ecosprin',dose:'Aspirin 150 mg',target:'COX-1 / thromboxane A₂',path:'Irreversible COX-1 acetylation → TXA₂ production ↓ → platelet aggregation ↓.',treat:'Reduces platelet-driven arterial thrombosis.',harm:'Bleeding and GI injury can occur because normal platelet hemostasis / prostaglandin pathways are also affected.',ilmb:'Improve upstream/downstream thrombogenic state, but no direct non-drug COX-1/TXA₂ replacement is established.',output:'TXB₂ / AA aggregation if clinically ordered',status:'DIRECT GAP REMAINS'},
{time:'Afternoon',name:'Seacap',dose:'Cod liver oil 300 mg total oil',target:'Mixed nutrient exposure',path:'Depends on actual EPA, DHA, vitamin A and vitamin D content on the product label.',treat:'Nutrient support only if chemistry matches a measured requirement.',harm:'Dose-dependent nutrient excess / interaction burden is possible.',ilmb:'Read exact label chemistry → chemical identity → measured requirement → response.',output:'Exact EPA/DHA/A/D input + relevant biomarkers',status:'CHEMISTRY NOT YET DEFINED'},
{time:'Afternoon',name:'Neurobion Forte',dose:'B-vitamin mixture',target:'Multiple vitamin-dependent pathways',path:'Supplies B-vitamin cofactors.',treat:'Corrects a deficiency only where a real requirement gap exists.',harm:'Unnecessary or excessive dosing can also create effects; exact formulation matters.',ilmb:'Requirement-first calculation from food / supplement chemistry for each nutrient.',output:'B12 and need-specific markers',status:'CONDITIONAL'},
{time:'Evening',name:'Lipvas 40',dose:'Atorvastatin 40 mg',target:'HMG-CoA reductase',path:'HMGCR inhibition → hepatic cholesterol synthesis ↓ → LDL receptor-mediated clearance ↑.',treat:'Lowers LDL / apoB-related vascular burden.',harm:'Possible muscle injury / myopathy and liver-enzyme elevation.',ilmb:'Food chemistry + intestinal sterol/fibre routes + activity/metabolic routes can lower the same output by different mechanisms.',output:'LDL / non-HDL / apoB',status:'PARTIAL'},
{time:'Evening',name:'Finobrate 160',dose:'Fenofibrate 160 mg',target:'PPARα',path:'PPARα activation → LPL / fatty-acid oxidation ↑ and TG-rich particle clearance ↑.',treat:'Lowers triglyceride / VLDL burden.',harm:'Liver, kidney, muscle and gallstone risk context matters.',ilmb:'Reduce TG production and increase utilisation through food chemistry, gut-metabolic and muscle-activity routes.',output:'Fasting triglycerides',status:'PARTIAL'}
];
const systems={brain:['Brain / right MCA','Known: right fronto-parieto-temporal ischemic injury with persistent severe right-MCA disease on later MRA. The unresolved question is current lumen, collateral reserve and tissue perfusion.'],blood:['Platelets / thrombosis','Clopidogrel directly changes P2Y12 signaling; aspirin directly changes COX-1/TXA₂. ILMB can improve background thrombogenic state but cannot currently claim direct receptor equivalence.'],heart:['Heart / vessels','Track blood pressure, resting heart rate, vascular resistance and endothelial function. Atenolol changes how heart-rate response should be interpreted during exercise.'],liver:['Liver / lipids','TG 301 mg/dL and ALT 81 U/L make lipid production/clearance and liver safety part of the same treatment picture.'],gut:['Gut / food chemistry','Food grams are converted to nutrients/chemicals; microbial and host pathways are mapped only where identities and coefficients are valid. Gut effects are modifiers, not substitutes for antiplatelet therapy.'],kidney:['Kidney / electrolytes','Creatinine 1.27, eGFR 72 and potassium 5.3 change the safety boundary for diet, supplements and medicines.'],motor:['Muscle / movement','Current function needs numbers: grip, strength, gait, sit-to-stand, dexterity, balance, ROM and tone. Rehab modules switch on only for measured deficits.'],thyroid:['Thyroid / metabolic context','TSH 5.386 should be interpreted with repeat TSH and free T4. This is part of the metabolic state, not automatically a causal explanation for the stroke.']};
let state=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ilmb_nilesh_v2')||'null')||{labs:{},bp:[],foods:[],text:{},motor:{},symptoms:{},decisions:{}};const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
document.querySelectorAll('nav button[data-tab]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>go(b.dataset.tab));document.querySelectorAll('[data-go]').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>go(x.dataset.go));function go(id){document.querySelectorAll('.section').forEach(s=>s.classList.remove('active'));document.querySelectorAll('nav button').forEach(b=>b.classList.remove('active'));$(id).classList.add('active');document.querySelector(`nav button[data-tab="${id}"]`)?.classList.add('active');scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})}
function renderMeds(){$('medList').innerHTML=meds.map((m,i)=>`<article class="card medicine"><div class="ey">${m.time}</div><h2>${m.name}</h2><span class="badge">${m.dose}</span><p><b>Target:</b> ${m.target}</p><div class="path"><b>Inside the body</b><br>${m.path}</div><div class="medgrid"><div class="medbox"><b>How it treats</b>${m.treat}</div><div class="medbox"><b>Collateral / side-effect path</b>${m.harm}</div><div class="medbox"><b>ILMB same-goal route</b>${m.ilmb}</div><div class="medbox"><b>How we measure the result</b>${m.output}</div></div><p><span class="badge ${m.status.includes('GAP')?'bad':'watch'}">${m.status}</span></p><label>What I actually experience</label><textarea data-med-note="${i}">${state.text['med'+i]||''}</textarea></article>`).join('')}
function renderLabs(){$('labRows').innerHTML=labs.map(l=>`<tr><td><b>${l[1]}</b></td><td>${l[2]} ${l[3]}</td><td>${l[4]}</td><td>${l[5]}</td><td><input type="number" step="any" data-lab="${l[0]}" value="${state.labs[l[0]]?.value||''}"></td><td><input type="date" data-lab-date="${l[0]}" value="${state.labs[l[0]]?.date||''}"></td><td><input data-lab-note="${l[0]}" value="${state.labs[l[0]]?.note||''}"></td></tr>`).join('')}
function renderBP(){$('bpLog').innerHTML=state.bp.map((r,i)=>`<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr 1fr 1fr auto;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px"><input type="datetime-local" data-bp-date="${i}" value="${r.date||''}"><input placeholder="SBP" data-bp-sbp="${i}" value="${r.sbp||''}"><input placeholder="DBP" data-bp-dbp="${i}" value="${r.dbp||''}"><input placeholder="HR" data-bp-hr="${i}" value="${r.hr||''}"><button class="btn" onclick="removeBP(${i})">×</button></div>`).join('')||'<p class="muted small">No readings entered yet.</p>'}function addBP(){state.bp.push({});saveAll(false);renderBP()}function removeBP(i){state.bp.splice(i,1);saveAll(false);renderBP()}
function renderFood(){$('foodLog').innerHTML=state.foods.map((r,i)=>`<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:110px 1.5fr 1fr 1fr auto;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px"><select data-food-day="${i}"><option ${r.day==='Day 1'?'selected':''}>Day 1</option><option ${r.day==='Day 2'?'selected':''}>Day 2</option><option ${r.day==='Day 3'?'selected':''}>Day 3</option></select><input placeholder="Food / drink" data-food-name="${i}" value="${r.name||''}"><input placeholder="grams / mL" data-food-qty="${i}" value="${r.qty||''}"><input placeholder="time / meal" data-food-time="${i}" value="${r.time||''}"><button class="btn" onclick="removeFood(${i})">×</button></div>`).join('')||'<p class="muted small">No foods entered yet.</p>'}function addFood(){state.foods.push({});saveAll(false);renderFood()}function removeFood(i){state.foods.splice(i,1);saveAll(false);renderFood()}
function renderReview(){const names=['Current medicines','Vascular-state workup','Food chemistry','BP / vascular conditioning','TG / lipid pathway','Motor rehabilitation','Vitamin D / nutrients','Sleep / autonomic state','Gut-metabolic route'];$('decisionRows').innerHTML=names.map(n=>`<div class="metric"><span>${n}</span><select data-decision="${n}" style="width:160px"><option>Not reviewed</option><option>KEEP</option><option>MODIFY</option><option>INVESTIGATE</option><option>ESCALATE</option><option>REMOVE</option></select></div>`).join('');const checks=['Current medicines taken as prescribed','7-day BP / HR log complete','Repeat fasting labs complete','Current MCA flow / collateral / perfusion question answered','Current DAPT indication / duration documented','Motor baseline complete','3-day weighed food log complete','Cod-liver-oil label chemistry entered','First controlled ILMB input period completed','Follow-up outputs remeasured'];$('checklist').innerHTML=checks.map((x,i)=>`<label><input type="checkbox" data-check="${i}" ${state.decisions['check'+i]?'checked':''}><span>${x}</span></label>`).join('')}
function openSys(k){$('drawerContent').innerHTML=`<div class="ey">MY BODY</div><h2>${systems[k][0]}</h2><p>${systems[k][1]}</p>`;$('drawer').classList.add('open')}function closeDrawer(){$('drawer').classList.remove('open')}
function collect(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-med-note]').forEach(el=>state.text['med'+el.dataset.medNote]=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-lab]').forEach(el=>{let k=el.dataset.lab;state.labs[k]=state.labs[k]||{};state.labs[k].value=el.value});document.querySelectorAll('[data-lab-date]').forEach(el=>{let k=el.dataset.labDate;state.labs[k]=state.labs[k]||{};state.labs[k].date=el.value});document.querySelectorAll('[data-lab-note]').forEach(el=>{let k=el.dataset.labNote;state.labs[k]=state.labs[k]||{};state.labs[k].note=el.value});document.querySelectorAll('[data-bp-date]').forEach(el=>{let i=+el.dataset.bpDate;state.bp[i]=state.bp[i]||{};state.bp[i].date=el.value});document.querySelectorAll('[data-bp-sbp]').forEach(el=>state.bp[+el.dataset.bpSbp].sbp=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-bp-dbp]').forEach(el=>state.bp[+el.dataset.bpDbp].dbp=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-bp-hr]').forEach(el=>state.bp[+el.dataset.bpHr].hr=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-food-day]').forEach(el=>state.foods[+el.dataset.foodDay].day=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-food-name]').forEach(el=>state.foods[+el.dataset.foodName].name=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-food-qty]').forEach(el=>state.foods[+el.dataset.foodQty].qty=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-food-time]').forEach(el=>state.foods[+el.dataset.foodTime].time=el.value);['reportNotes','bodyNotes','symptomNotes','motorGoals','responseNotes'].forEach(id=>state.text[id]=$(id)?.value||'');['leftGrip','rightGrip','walk10','sitstand','leftArm','rightArm','leftLeg','rightLeg'].forEach(id=>state.motor[id]=$(id)?.value||'');['bleeding','dizziness','fatigue','muscle'].forEach(id=>state.symptoms[id]=$(id)?.value||'');document.querySelectorAll('[data-decision]').forEach(el=>state.decisions[el.dataset.decision]=el.value);document.querySelectorAll('[data-check]').forEach(el=>state.decisions['check'+el.dataset.check]=el.checked)}
function saveAll(show=true){collect();localStorage.setItem('ilmb_nilesh_v2',JSON.stringify(state));if(show)alert('Saved on this device.')}function exportData(){saveAll(false);const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify({patient:'Nilesh Yadav',exportedAt:new Date().toISOString(),entries:state},null,2)],{type:'application/json'}));a.download='Nilesh_ILMB_entries.json';a.click();URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href)}
function hydrate(){renderMeds();renderLabs();renderBP();renderFood();renderReview();['reportNotes','bodyNotes','symptomNotes','motorGoals','responseNotes'].forEach(id=>{if($(id))$(id).value=state.text[id]||''});['leftGrip','rightGrip','walk10','sitstand','leftArm','rightArm','leftLeg','rightLeg'].forEach(id=>{if($(id))$(id).value=state.motor[id]||''});['bleeding','dizziness','fatigue','muscle'].forEach(id=>{if($(id))$(id).value=state.symptoms[id]||'No'});document.querySelectorAll('[data-decision]').forEach(el=>{if(state.decisions[el.dataset.decision])el.value=state.decisions[el.dataset.decision]})}hydrate();
</script></body></html>